<title>FRANCE: MOTOR RACING-LANGTON SUSTAINS SERIOUS HEAD INJURIES.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-LANGTON SUSTAINS SERIOUS HEAD INJURIES.</headline>
<dateline>NOGARO, France 1996-10-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Briton Soames Langton was airlifted to hospital with serious head injuries on Saturday after his Porche crashed on the ninth and penultimate round of the world endurance championship.</p>
<p>Officials on Sunday said Langton, 28, was unconscious in intensive care in a hospital in Mont-de-Marsan.</p>
